\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Where the single-edge chain meets published comparisons}
\date{2026-11-21}

\p{The sign comparisons of \ref{fdip-0128} record two
infinite-volume discussions, and \ref{fdip-0118} records the
fixed-length model among them. \ref{fdip-0129} compares the
continuous doublet orbit with two finite orbits. The frame
eigenvalues of \ref{fdip-012G} are eigenvalues of a finite
orbit matrix under the Rayleigh hypothesis. The onsite values
in \ref{fdip-013B} and \ref{fdip-013D} are the Yukawa step of
this chain. \ref{fdip-011O} gives the sign vanishing and the
exchange eigenvalues. The positivity hypothesis of
\ref{fdip-011V} remains the condition for a positive definite
fermion kernel. The quotient group of \ref{fdip-0126} remains a
finite group.}
